47fl|v|To make a low, prolonged sound, like that of a bee in flight; to drone; to murmur; to buzz; as, a top hums. ; To make a nasal sound, like that of the letter m prolonged, without opening the mouth, or articulating; to mumble in monotonous undertone; to drone. ; To make an inarticulate sound, like h'm, through the nose in the process of speaking, from embarrassment or a affectation; to hem. ; To express satisfaction by a humming noise. ; To have the sensation of a humming noise; as, my head hums, -- a pathological condition. ; To sing with shut mouth; to murmur without articulation; to mumble; as, to hum a tune. ; To express satisfaction with by humming. ; To flatter by approving; to cajole; to impose on; to humbug.	o:74id,31,1;9hzy,18,1;2h4e,18,1~9hzy,18,1;2h4e,18,1;74id,31,1	s:5i2g,80,57;9t6i,73,21;362j,21,1;7tp1,15,2~5i2g,80,57;9t6i,73,21;7tp1,15,2;362j,21,1	d:n1f,76,1;5z3h,1,3~5z3h,1,3;n1f,76,1	D:n1f,106,8;5eje,68,4;aq7,34,59~aq7,34,59;n1f,106,8;5eje,68,4
